WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.561 --> 00:00:18.612
"I still can't believe Mrs.

2
00:00:18.732 --> 00:00:22.235
Smith left her glasses in her bird feeder," Henry said.

3
00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:24.596
"I know."

4
00:00:25.057 --> 00:00:26.318
His cousin Maggie laughed.

5
00:00:26.338 --> 00:00:29.300
"She's lucky a bird didn't peck them."

6
00:00:30.224 --> 00:00:35.289
"No, she's lucky that The Lemonade Detectives were around to track them down for her," said Henry's friend

7
00:00:35.389 --> 00:00:42.375
Cole. The Lemonade Detectives had been in business all summer.

8
00:00:43.396 --> 00:00:45.017
They'd solved lots of cases.

9
00:00:45.978 --> 00:00:48.821
Some cases were pretty simple, like finding Mrs.

10
00:00:48.881 --> 00:00:50.222
Smith's lost glasses.

11
00:00:51.743 --> 00:00:53.064
Other cases were trickier.

12
00:00:53.825 --> 00:00:56.908
But so far The Lemonade Detectives had solved them all.

13
00:00:59.276 --> 00:01:00.477
"Here come some customers."

14
00:01:01.998 --> 00:01:04.759
Henry saw two teenage girls walking toward them.

15
00:01:04.779 --> 00:01:09.962
"I wonder whether they want to buy lemonade or hire us to solve a mystery."

16
00:01:09.982 --> 00:01:12.284
"It's a mystery to me!"

17
00:01:12.724 --> 00:01:13.785
Cole joked with a grin.

18
00:01:13.805 --> 00:01:17.207
"Not to me," Maggie said, smiling.

19
00:01:17.227 --> 00:01:22.410
"Ashley and Jill buy at least one cup of lemonade apiece almost every day!"

20
00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:26.112
Sure enough the older girls ordered two lemonades.

21
00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:31.742
While Maggie was pouring their drinks, Ashley took a piece of paper out of her pocket.

22
00:01:31.762 --> 00:01:34.324
"Are you guys busy next Saturday?"

23
00:01:34.604 --> 00:01:35.745
She held out the paper.

24
00:01:35.765 --> 00:01:39.867
"Because we're having a fundraiser for the Belltown High School soccer team."

25
00:01:39.887 --> 00:01:42.628
"Ugh!" Cole groaned.

26
00:01:42.648 --> 00:01:44.830
"Don't talk about school!

27
00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:47.131
It's still summer, remember?"

28
00:01:47.151 --> 00:01:50.793
"Only for a few more weeks," Henry said.

29
00:01:51.713 --> 00:01:52.614
Ashley laughed.

30
00:01:52.634 --> 00:01:53.954
"I know.

31
00:01:54.695 --> 00:01:56.436
That's why we're holding the fundraiser."

32
00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:58.280
Jill nodded.

33
00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:02.142
"We're raising money before school starts so we can get new uniforms."

34
00:02:03.282 --> 00:02:04.483
Henry looked at the paper.

35
00:02:05.723 --> 00:02:13.567
It said: BELLTOWN HIGH SCHOOL FUNDRAISER Enjoy the end of summer with a bike ride through beautiful Belltown

36
00:02:13.627 --> 00:02:23.831
Park All profits used to support the girls' soccer team $10 per person, snacks provided Cole was reading

37
00:02:23.911 --> 00:02:25.031
over Henry's shoulder.

38
00:02:25.051 --> 00:02:27.585
"Wow. That sounds cool.

39
00:02:28.385 --> 00:02:29.987
I love biking on those trails."

40
00:02:30.007 --> 00:02:33.149
"You can keep the flyer," Ashley said.

41
00:02:33.169 --> 00:02:38.073
"If you decide to come, just bring your bike, a helmet, and ten dollars."

42
00:02:43.638 --> 00:02:46.280
Then she and Jill wandered off with their lemonade.

43
00:02:48.842 --> 00:02:50.703
Cole was still looking at the flyer.

44
00:02:50.723 --> 00:02:52.705
"We're going, right?"

45
00:02:53.045 --> 00:02:53.505
he said.

46
00:02:53.525 --> 00:02:56.448
"I'd like to do it," Henry said.

47
00:02:57.316 --> 00:03:00.098
"It sounds like fun, and it's for a good cause."

48
00:03:00.118 --> 00:03:02.539
"What about the lemonade stand?"

49
00:03:02.899 --> 00:03:03.640
Maggie asked.

50
00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:08.422
"We probably won't have many customers that day anyway," Cole pointed out.

51
00:03:08.442 --> 00:03:10.943
"Lots of kids will be at the park."

52
00:03:11.984 --> 00:03:13.985
"Maybe you're right," Maggie said.

53
00:03:14.005 --> 00:03:17.527
"Besides we made lots of money this week.

54
00:03:18.407 --> 00:03:20.869
I guess we can donate some of it to a good cause."

55
00:03:24.831 --> 00:03:26.332
It was the day of the fundraiser.

56
00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:36.381
The Lemonade Detectives had just ridden their bikes into Belltown Park.

57
00:03:39.462 --> 00:03:42.102
"Wow. There are tons of people here!"

58
00:03:42.403 --> 00:03:43.263
Cole exclaimed.

59
00:03:47.664 --> 00:03:49.324
looks like we sign in over there."

60
00:03:50.325 --> 00:03:54.726
Maggie pointed to a table draped with Belltown High School's colors, blue and white.

61
00:03:55.686 --> 00:03:59.147
Ashley and Jill were sitting behind the table with some of their teammates.

62
00:04:00.127 --> 00:04:01.168
Henry walked over.

63
00:04:01.188 --> 00:04:04.085
"Hi. We're here to ride."

64
00:04:04.105 --> 00:04:06.767
"Great!" Jill smiled.

65
00:04:07.507 --> 00:04:08.708
"Ten dollars each, please."

66
00:04:09.729 --> 00:04:11.730
Henry and his friends handed over their money.

67
00:04:12.871 --> 00:04:15.153
In exchange, Jill handed each of them a ticket.

68
00:04:15.173 --> 00:04:18.635
"Make sure you don't lose those," she said.

69
00:04:18.655 --> 00:04:22.118
"Everyone who finishes the ride gets a T-shirt at the end."

70
00:04:22.138 --> 00:04:25.220
"Really?" Maggie looked surprised.

71
00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:27.682
"How can you afford that?

72
00:04:28.803 --> 00:04:30.264
I thought you were trying to raise money."

73
00:04:31.588 --> 00:04:33.008
Ashley heard her and looked over.

74
00:04:33.028 --> 00:04:38.370
"The T-shirts are being donated by Belltown Bikes," she said.

75
00:04:38.390 --> 00:04:40.591
"They're our sponsor."

76
00:04:41.851 --> 00:04:44.972
She pointed to a sign advertising the local bicycle shop.

77
00:04:45.832 --> 00:04:48.193
Meanwhile Henry heard someone calling his name.

78
00:04:49.353 --> 00:04:50.754
It was his friend Nathan.

79
00:04:50.774 --> 00:04:53.534
"Are you guys riding too?"

80
00:04:53.914 --> 00:04:54.735
Nathan asked.

81
00:04:54.755 --> 00:04:56.855
"Yeah," Cole said.

82
00:04:56.875 --> 00:04:59.196
"Just like everybody else in town!"

83
00:05:00.084 --> 00:05:03.286
"And some people from out of town too," Maggie added.

84
00:05:03.306 --> 00:05:06.769
"Look! Isn't that a Valley High T-shirt?"

85
00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:11.412
She pointed to a teenage boy wearing a red-and-gold Valley High shirt.

86
00:05:12.553 --> 00:05:15.075
Valley High was the high school in a neighboring town.

87
00:05:16.075 --> 00:05:18.017
Nathan pointed in a different direction.

88
00:05:18.037 --> 00:05:22.580
"That dark-haired girl Tina goes to Valley High too," he said.

89
00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:25.442
"She babysits my little sister sometimes."

90
00:05:25.462 --> 00:05:27.924
"That's weird," Cole said.

91
00:05:29.080 --> 00:05:32.542
"Why would people from Valley High want to raise money for Belltown?

92
00:05:33.422 --> 00:05:34.823
They're our biggest rivals!"

93
00:05:34.843 --> 00:05:38.405
"If you think that's weird, look at that guy."

94
00:05:39.626 --> 00:05:41.927
Maggie was staring at a man standing by himself.

95
00:05:43.368 --> 00:05:45.789
Most of the riders were kids or teenagers.

96
00:05:46.749 --> 00:05:49.911
The adults were mostly teachers or coaches from Belltown High.

97
00:05:50.832 --> 00:05:52.913
But Henry didn't recognize this man.

98
00:05:53.893 --> 00:05:57.875
He was in his twenties, with very broad shoulders and dark sunglasses.

99
00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:02.061
"Maybe he just likes bike riding," Henry said.

100
00:06:02.081 --> 00:06:05.583
"He doesn't look very happy to be here," Cole said.

101
00:06:05.603 --> 00:06:08.545
"He's not smiling or talking to anyone."

102
00:06:09.505 --> 00:06:11.746
Just then someone shouted for attention.

103
00:06:12.867 --> 00:06:13.447
It was Ms.

104
00:06:13.487 --> 00:06:15.908
Hernandez, the girls' soccer coach.

105
00:06:15.928 --> 00:06:19.070
"Is everyone ready to have some fun?"

106
00:06:19.530 --> 00:06:20.070
she called.

107
00:06:21.151 --> 00:06:23.152
That made Henry forget about everything else.

108
00:06:27.982 --> 00:06:29.556
The ride was about to start!
